{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Upon [your walls, O Jerusalem, I have set watchmen].</b> These watchmen are a designation for the mourners of Zion, who have no occupation but weeping, and they do not sleep at night, like the watchmen of the walls." "And he added <b>all the day</b>, for the custom of watchmen is to sleep by day, and thus it is written: \"My soul waits for Adonai\" (Psalms 130:6) [(Jonah 2:9)]. And so the prophet explained his words: for <b>they remind</b> is a verb with two objects, like \"make me remember; let us judge together\" (Isaiah 43:26):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {1 "The second parenthetical citation appears in the small-print source as (יונה ב' ט'), i.e., Jonah 2:9; I have rendered it but left it in brackets to indicate it is a secondary citation within the flow."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:42.667021051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}